# oracle: fix hmc with the rigid keyword (fix rigid/small molecule SPC/E water of examples/mc/in.hmc.rigid, replicated 2x2x2 instead of 4x4x4): 50 rigid steps, then 4 HMC moves of 10 steps at a 3 fs timestep (the bodies' momenta resampled per body in the native storage order; a rejection brings the bodies back), with the acceptance vector
# Tolerance: the 24-atom box (4.8 A under a 9 A cutoff) runs hot at a 3 fs timestep, and its chaos amplifies 1e-13
# differences (rows agree to 1e-13 at the HMC setup, 1e-10 ten steps later); the energy changes f_2[3..5] are small
# differences of large energies.
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.9e-6 (f_2[5]; temp 2.7e-8), atoms 1.8e-7.
# oracle-examples: mc/data.hmc.spce
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-5
units           real
boundary        p p p
atom_style      full
read_data       data.hmc.spce
replicate       2 2 2
mass            1 15.9994
mass            2 1.00784
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long 9.0
pair_modify     tail yes mix arithmetic
kspace_style    pppm 1.0e-5
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1554015 3.166
pair_coeff      2 2 0 0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 554.1349 1.000
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 45.7696 109.47
timestep        1.0
thermo          25
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
fix             1 all rigid/small molecule
run             50
timestep        3.0
fix             2 all hmc 10 654123 300.0 rigid 1
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal press f_2 f_2[*]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             40
